      "18726": {
        "comments": [
          {
            "creator": "kevinushey",
            "creation_time": "2024-05-08T18:09:35Z",
            "text": "`setTimeLimit(transient = TRUE)` is a useful tool for limiting the amount of time R can spend running some chunk of code. However, the errors emitted on timeout are just \"regular\" errors, e.g.\n\n```\n> result <- tryCatch({\n+    setTimeLimit(elapsed = 1L, transient = TRUE)\n+    Sys.sleep(2)\n+ }, error = identity)\n> result\n<simpleError in Sys.sleep(2): reached elapsed time limit>\n```\n\nIt would be useful if these errors had a custom class set, so that one could specifically detect and handle these errors -- similar to how R now uses the `stackOverflowError` class for stack overflow errors.",
            "bug_id": 18726,
            "count": 0,
            "is_markdown": true,
            "tags": [],
            "attachment_id": {},
            "time": "2024-05-08T18:09:35Z",
            "id": 100849,
            "is_private": false
          },
          {
            "tags": [],
            "is_private": false,
            "id": 102417,
            "creation_time": "2025-11-20T17:17:13Z",
            "count": 1,
            "text": "Created attachment 3563\nSpecial function in error.c for checking the Time Limit\n\nThe patch is related adding a special Time Limit Error function for R_checkTimeLimit(), as mentioned in the https://github.com/r-devel/r-dev-day/issues/114#issue-3393407665  issue",
            "bug_id": 18726,
            "attachment_id": 3563,
            "time": "2025-11-20T17:17:13Z",
            "creator": "siddheshakole",
            "is_markdown": true
          },
          {
            "creator": "michael.lydeamore",
            "is_markdown": true,
            "attachment_id": 3564,
            "time": "2025-11-21T02:11:01Z",
            "creation_time": "2025-11-21T02:11:01Z",
            "count": 2,
            "text": "Created attachment 3564\nClassed Errors for timeouts diffs\n\nFrom the R Dev Day in November.\n\nThoughts are to use a hierarchical error system:\n\nTimeoutError is the superclass that can be used more generally across the broad.\n\nThe four errors currently thrown by R are considered TimeLimit*TimeoutErrors in the patch. These are then broken down into CPU/non-CPU and session/non-session.\n\nSome re-implementation of getCurrentCall() was needed to be able to return the call back to the user.",
            "bug_id": 18726,
            "tags": [],
            "is_private": false,
            "id": 102418
          }
        ]
      }
    }
